-- title:
--   Newform behind a point of the ordinary local Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring, a domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field $k$, let $p \ne 2$ be a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a $2$-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline k$). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $N \ne 0$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p \mid N$ but $p^2 \nmid N$, and such that the integral lattice in the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ spans them over $\mathbb C$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,N\,2\,S$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ generated by the Hecke operators away from $S$) to $k$ such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Assume further that the adic Galois representation attached to $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$: for every valuation subring over $p$ there is a line $L = k\cdot b_0$ spanned by a member of a basis of $V$, stable under the decomposition group, with inertia acting trivially modulo $L$. Finally let $\mathcal O'$ be a second such complete characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring domain with finite residue field, module-finite over $\mathcal O$ by a local algebra map, and let $\psi$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the localised Hecke algebra $\mathrm{heckeLocal}\,N\,S\,\mathcal O\,\theta$ (the localisation of the Hecke algebra at the submonoid determined by $\theta$) to $\mathcal O'$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a further complete characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring domain $\mathcal O''$ with finite residue field, module-finite over $\mathcal O$ by a local algebra map, an injective $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : \mathcal O' \to \mathcal O''$, a nonzero divisor $M_g$ of $N$, a weight-two cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform whose good eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor of $M_g$), a ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from the full Hecke algebra of level $M_g$ (no excluded primes) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)$ the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ for every prime $\ell \nmid M_g$ and $\chi_g(U_q)$ the $q$-th coefficient for every prime $q \mid M_g$, and a ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O''$, such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ one has $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell)) = \varphi(\psi(\pi(T_\ell)))$, $\pi$ being the localisation map, and such that, in case $p \nmid M_g$, the element $\iota(\chi_g(T_p))$ is a unit of $\mathcal O''$. Nothing is asserted about $T_p$ or $U_p$ when $p \mid M_g$.
--
--   This is the per-point statement of the local analysis at an ordinary prime exactly dividing the level: a point of the $\theta$-local Hecke algebra with values in a finite complete discrete valuation ring comes from a newform of level dividing $N$ whose Hecke eigenvalues away from $S$ match the point, and whose $p$-th eigenvalue is a $p$-adic unit in the $p$-old case, the supersingular $p$-old alternative being excluded by ordinariness of $\bar\rho$. It feeds the statement that, after passing to an algebraic closure, all such points are accounted for by newforms with unit root at $p$.
